                                        "entry_id": "33381c33-dd08-3875-9dd9-f872124ba08b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Engaging in the creation of a conworld; worldbuilding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "uncommon",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb509866-6371-4d1f-a241-985a8326e674",
                                                "sense_id": "0a8e61a0-4367-3699-a070-e392323a5d46",
                                                "text": "[responding to \"Aren't you the God and Creator of the Kigdatsi?\"] Not a god, but I thought them up, though I was trying to keep that quiet. Did you search the web for \"Kigdatsi\"? Also, I am *not* a sci-fi author, just a person who likes conworlding."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea33f464-9b07-4420-a21a-eb071ad2961e",
                                                "sense_id": "0a8e61a0-4367-3699-a070-e392323a5d46",
                                                "text": "For those who are not familiar with the term, conworlding is the art of world building. It is the concept of creating an imaginary world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5a9547-6580-4a7b-82b8-b6d60b694008",
                                                "sense_id": "0a8e61a0-4367-3699-a070-e392323a5d46",
                                                "text": "Otherwise known as 'subcreation' or 'conworlding' (constructed worlds), the success of these fabrications relies on their consistent upholding of self-instigated internal rules and logic systems."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
